@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@ Rules below are law for every agent, every session. Format: imperative + enforci
 15. **Every gold/silver/bronze `.py` begins with `from __future__ import annotations`** (PEP-604 on py3.9 runners). Gate-enforced (ADHC_DSFLOW.004).
 16. **Local-runtime bash uses only Git Bash 3.6.7 default-install utilities.** MISSING (guarded `command -v` fallback required): `pgrep pkill flock pidof setsid wget` — canonical fallback pattern: `org/mcp/inbox-watch.sh`. EC2-side scripts exempt (Amazon Linux). `docs/architecture/ADHC_BASHFIX.md`.
 17. **Silver = dedup + dtype standardization ONLY. NEVER slim fields, NEVER fillna/dropna/business-row-filter, NEVER drop bronze columns** — anything needing judgment about field relevance or null meaning is gold-tier business logic. Legacy violators migrate to passthrough on next touch. Permitted/forbidden lists + Andrew directive: `memory/feedback_silver_no_field_slimming.md`.
+17a. **BRONZE IS RAW AND UNTOUCHED — whatever the source delivers (`.gz` / `.json` / `.csv`), byte-for-byte. PARQUET IS A *SILVER* FORMAT: the universal parquet conversion is part of silver's cleaning + standardization, NEVER of ingest.** A `.parquet` under `bronze/` is an **architectural violation, not a format preference** — it imposes a schema and coerces dtypes AT INGEST, so whatever the raw feed carried that the conversion dropped is **not recoverable**, and bronze's one job (everything downstream is re-derivable) is destroyed. **This is Rule 17's spine one layer up: each layer has exactly one job, and DOING A LATER LAYER'S JOB EARLY IS IRREVERSIBLE.** Silver may not do gold's judgment; **bronze may not do silver's conversion.** **Gate candidate (CTO to route):** a commit/deploy-time lint denying any `.parquet` write whose key starts `bronze/`, + a periodic S3 sweep of every `bronze/` prefix for non-raw extensions. **>> AND THE TRAP THAT MAKES THIS A RULE AND NOT A NOTE: WHEN THE DEPLOYED CODE AND THE REPO DISAGREE, "WHICH ONE IS RUNNING?" IS THE WRONG QUESTION — "WHICH ONE IS *RIGHT*?" IS, AND THAT IS AN ARCHITECTURAL QUESTION NO MEASUREMENT CAN ANSWER.** I censused the INF forks, found the deployed Lambdas writing `bronze/*.parquet` against a canonical `.jsonl.gz`, ruled *"deployed wins, the repo is stale"*, and routed DS to change `data/` — **which would have cemented the violation into the canonical repo with a ratification on it. The fix was the defect. I mistook the RUNTIME for the STANDARD.** (Andrew-direct 2026-07-13; live consequence: the raw bronze ingest for `positions` + `assets` **stopped 2026-07-10** — three days with no re-derivable layer.) Why/verbatim: `memory/feedback_bronze_is_raw_untouched_parquet_is_a_silver_conversion.md`.
 18. **`terraform apply` goes through `.tools/safe-apply.sh`** — HALTGT inbox checkpoint at the last reversible moment (routine pending msg → `HALT_ACK=1`; override audited via `HALT_OVERRIDE="reason"`). **A HALTGT PASS IS NOT EVIDENCE YOU WERE NOT HALTED, and `[STOP]` does NOT reliably hard-block** — the checkpoint sees only *unread* files directly under `inbox/<serial>/`, so a live Monitor (which moves the message first) guarantees a silent empty-inbox `exit 0`, and a `~lane` agent is unhaltable regardless. **Latch repair pending; NOBODY CITES A HALTGT PASS.** `docs/architecture/ADHC_HALTGT.md`, `org/tier0/ledger/LD-0267.md`.
 19. **Portal main worktree stays on `DEV`, always.** Promotes run in an ephemeral worktree (`/prod-deploy` skill, DT lane). Found it on PROD? `cd portal && git checkout DEV` before any portal work — never work around via `.runtmp` copies. `docs/briefs/portal-main-tree-stays-on-dev-rule-20260526.md`.
 20. **Check the dependency graph BEFORE you change anything** — (a) ahead of ANY cloud/infra/data change; (b) before commit for ANY frontend change. Pick the tool from `org/modules/graph/graph-call-manifest.yaml`. **Default to QUERY, never rebuild to answer a traversal** (`comp-kuzu` auto-refreshes on HEAD-advance). **Read the provenance header on every call** — `UNKNOWN VINTAGE` = freshness unverifiable; a scratch DB (`--db-path`) is a frozen vintage, never quote one as "the estate". Verify your OWN just-made change against live AWS/served artifacts, never the graph. **`comp-surface-check` IS NOT A GATE — IT CANNOT BLOCK.** It prints `CRITICAL ... SEV1` and the commit proceeds; and it is structurally blind to the SEV1 surfaces anyway (they live in the `portal/` submodule, which `safe-commit` cannot see). **Nothing gates them — run it BY HAND, read its output yourself, and never treat silence or an unblocked commit as a pass.** Blocking fix arch-gated to CTO — `org/tier0/ledger/LD-0273.md`. Design: `docs/architecture/NFRA_GRAPHS.md`.
